     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Sunday, February 1, 2015 at 8:36:28 PM UTC-8, Bill Evans wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><ul style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\"><b>Date</b>: Friday, Feb 27</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\"><b>Time</b>: <strike>4:30pm</strike> <span style=\"color:rgb(255,0,0)\">5:15pm</span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\"><b>Location</b>: MIIS, <strike>actual room TBD</strike> <span style=\"color:rgb(255,0,0)\">McGowan Building, room MG001 (<a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir//36.5999464,-121.8957709/@36.5999232,-121.8958983,20z/data=!4m2!4m1!3e0\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.google.com/maps/dir//36.5999464,-121.8957709/@36.5999232,-121.8958983,20z/data%3D!4m2!4m1!3e0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793247167910000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nbmXkht9PXeChZP_fEaLF\">map</a>)<br></span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\"><b>Topic</b>: Data Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">For many, “data management” consists of basic subsetting and sorting an R <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">data.frame</code>. However, when it comes time to do level-specific processing or merging the data with another <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">data.frame</code>, we often resort to bringing it back into a spreadsheet, manually band-aiding things together, and eventually bringing it back into R for the statistical analysis. Let’s discuss ways we can do all of this in R, easier and faster.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Subtopics:</p>\r\n<ul style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Review basic <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">data.frame</code> subsetting and management within R;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Row-wise operations using <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">foreach</code> and <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">iterators</code>, facilitating simple parallelization in a multi-core or cluster environment;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Use of <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">dplyr</code> and <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">tidyr</code> for row-wise operations, group-wise operations, summarizing, and complex merging;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Dealing with large numbers of data files, e.g., a directory full of CSVs for aggregate or sequential analysis.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"><i>(For those who came in January to the “(Relative) (Re)Introduction to R”, this will be an expansion of the middle section, somewhere between “apply” and “multi-plot graphic layout options”.)</i></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdiBkaXI9Imx0ciI+PGRpdiBkaXI9Imx0ciI+KiAqKkRhdGUqKjogRnJpZGF5LCBGZWIgMjc8\r\nYnI+PGJyPiogKipUaW1lKio6ICZsdDtzdHJpa2UmZ3Q7NDozMHBtJmx0Oy9zdHJpa2UmZ3Q7IDU6\r\nMTVwbTxicj48YnI+KiAqKkxvY2F0aW9uKio6IE1JSVMsICZsdDtzdHJpa2UmZ3Q7YWN0dWFsIHJv\r\nb20gVEJEJmx0Oy9zdHJpa2UmZ3Q7IE1jR293YW4gQnVpbGRpbmcsIHJvb20gTUcwMDE8YnI+PGJy\r\nPiogKipUb3BpYyoqOiBEYXRhIE1hbmFnZW1lbnQ8YnI+PGJyPkZvciBtYW55LCAiZGF0YSBtYW5h\r\nZ2VtZW50IiBjb25zaXN0cyBvZiBiYXNpYyBzdWJzZXR0aW5nIGFuZCBzb3J0aW5nIGFuIFIgYGRh\r\ndGEuZnJhbWVgLiBIb3dldmVyLCB3aGVuIGl0IGNvbWVzIHRpbWUgdG8gZG8gbGV2ZWwtc3BlY2lm\r\naWMgcHJvY2Vzc2luZyBvciBtZXJnaW5nIHRoZSBkYXRhIHdpdGggYW5vdGhlciBgZGF0YS5mcmFt\r\nZWAsIHdlIG9mdGVuIHJlc29ydCB0byBicmluZ2luZyBpdCBiYWNrIGludG8gYSBzcHJlYWRzaGVl\r\ndCwgbWFudWFsbHkgYmFuZC1haWRpbmcgdGhpbmdzIHRvZ2V0aGVyLCBhbmQgZXZlbnR1YWxseSBi\r\ncmluZ2luZyBpdCBiYWNrIGludG8gUiBmb3IgdGhlIHN0YXRpc3RpY2FsIGFuYWx5c2lzLiBMZXQn\r\ncyBkaXNjdXNzIHdheXMgd2UgY2FuIGRvIGFsbCBvZiB0aGlzIGluIFIsIGVhc2llciBhbmQgZmFz\r\ndGVyLjxicj48YnI+U3VidG9waWNzOjxicj48YnI+KiBSZXZpZXcgYmFzaWMgYGRhdGEuZnJhbWVg\r\nIHN1YnNldHRpbmcgYW5kIG1hbmFnZW1lbnQgd2l0aGluIFI7PGJ