     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Thanks, Fernando! Attached are the three scripts:</p>\r\n<ul style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">dataStructs.R</code> provides the functions used to automate the walk-through in <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">rglstuff.R</code>;</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">rglstuff.R</code> is a walk-through, trying to provide visualization of different data structures. Though it’s not very self-documenting, most of the examples show the code that is being depicted. I have some thoughts on how to improve this, and will likely be improving this in the future on the groups <a href=\"https://github.com/GRUMP\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/GRUMP&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793247167913000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2OKagGPfA3WRJXmXM-hgNJ\">Github site</a> (project forthcoming).</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">notes.R</code> is the remainder of the talk, walking through the R functions of *<code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">apply</code>, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">dplyr</code>, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">tidyr</code>, etc.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Questions, comments, suggestions, and pull-requests are welcome!</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">-r2</p></div></div>"
    ],
